Q: Why do I get different results from other languages when mixing bitwise and arithmetic operators? A: <p>You can do this to make it work like in C#</p>

<pre><code>var j = 0x783a9b23;
var bt = ((16843134 ^ (16843134 - 1)) * j);
bt = bt % 2147483647
</code></pre>

<p>This is because in c# your integer overflows the limit of 2,147,483,647.</p>
